10. STAGE 1 — AUTOMATIC READINESS
==================================================

When both context selections are available:
- Start readiness for the exact:
  calculation ID + sector ID + scenario ID.
- Highlight Readiness blue and Running.
- Keep other stages Pending.
- Keep Calculate disabled.

Prevent duplicate checks for an unchanged selection.
Cancel or ignore stale responses after selection changes.

Under Readiness, display individual checks as statement-style activities.

Applicable checks may include:
- Calculation enabled for the selected scenario.
- Required workstream/input data available.
- Actuals validated where required.
- Workstream unlocked.
- No conflicting job already running.
- Required template/mapping available.
- Changed configuration or recalculation requirement.
- Calculation-specific prerequisite artifacts.

Use the detailed readiness reference as a presentation guide.
Only display checks applicable to the selected calculation and returned
by the backend.

For example:
- A pretax-report prerequisite should apply to Net Income Tax only if
  required by its backend rules.
- Do not impose it on Tax ETR without a corresponding business requirement.

Each check displays:
- Backend-provided check name or statement.
- Spinner while running.
- Checkmark when satisfied.
- Failure icon and reason when blocked.
- Warning indicator for non-blocking warnings.

Warnings are not automatically blocking failures.
Use backend readiness decisions and severity.

When readiness passes:
- Mark Readiness Completed.
- Show:
  “The selected sector and scenario meet the required configuration checks.
   You can proceed with the calculation.”
- Enable Calculate.
- Leave the other stages Pending.
- Do not automatically start execution.

When readiness fails:
- Mark Readiness Failed.
- Keep Calculate disabled.
- Show the actual failed prerequisites and corrective guidance.
- Provide Retry Readiness.

When the readiness request fails:
- Show:
  “Unable to verify readiness. Please retry.”
- Distinguish request failure from failed business prerequisites.
- Keep Calculate disabled.

If the backend reports an existing active run:
- Restore that run where supported.
- Do not offer duplicate execution.

